# SecondChance structured breed reference
# Produced by an LLM labeling pass (Claude, Anthropic) over the 254 atomic breed
# tokens that appear in Austin Animal Center intake records between 2013-10-01
# and 2022-03-04. The production pipeline regenerates this file by calling the
# same model through Amazon Bedrock; see src/secondchance/labeling/breed_llm.py.
#
# Columns: name|group|size|weight_lb|coat|grooming|energy|flags
#   group    SP Sporting, HO Hound, WK Working, TE Terrier, TO Toy,
#            NS Non-Sporting, HE Herding, FSS AKC Foundation Stock Service,
#            NR not recognized by AKC (landrace, type name, or shorthand),
#            CD domestic cat (non-pedigree), CP pedigree cat
#   size     T toy, S small, M medium, L large, G giant
#   coat     H hairless, S short, M medium, L long
#   grooming L low, M moderate, H high
#   energy   L low, M moderate, H high, V very high
#   flags    5 binary digits in order:
#            bully_type, brachycephalic, guardian_or_working, bsl_risk, recognized_purebred
#            bsl_risk marks breeds commonly named in US breed specific legislation
#            or in homeowner insurance exclusion lists. It is recorded because it
#            plausibly affects adopter demand, never as a reason to withhold care.
